{
"note_claim": "Congress explicitly granted the executive branch the authority to designate, extend, or terminate Temporary Protected Status (TPS) under 8 U.S. Code § 1254a",
"label": "SUPPORTS",
"quote": "The Attorney General , after consultation with appropriate agencies of the Government, may designate any foreign state (or any part of such foreign state) under this subsection",
"reason": "The statute text explicitly authorizes the Attorney General (executive branch) to designate foreign states for TPS under this code section."
}
